  "response": "## Analyse\nJe vais implémenter une fixture `initial_state` dans `tests/test_integration.py` qui charge un état initial via un state manager avec fallback stub. La fixture utilisera le pattern `robust_import_with_stub` et inclura une assertion immédiate pour valider l'état chargé.\n\n```python path: tests/test_integration.py\nimport pytest\nimport sys\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n# Add project root to path for imports\nproject_root = Path(__file__).parent.parent\nsys.path.insert(0, str(project_root))\n\n# Robust import with stub fallback\ntry:\n    from src.state_manager import StateManager\n    from src.models import State\nexcept ImportError:\n    # Stub fallback when modules don't exist yet\n    class State:\n        def __init__(self):\n            self.iteration = 0\n            self.phase = \"INIT\"\n            self.skills = {}\n            self.learnings = []\n            self.confidence = 0.0\n    \n    class StateManager:\n        def load_state(self, path=None):\n            return State()\n        \n        def save_state(self, state, path=None):\n            pass\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef initial_state():\n    \"\"\"Fixture qui charge l'état initial du système.\n    \n    Returns:\n        State: Objet d'état valide avec attributs initialisés\n    \"\"\"\n    state_manager = StateManager()\n    state = state_manager.load_state()\n    \n    # Assertion immédiate pour valider le contrat\n    assert state.iteration is not None, \"L'état doit avoir un numéro d'itération\"\n    assert hasattr(state, 'phase'), \"L'état doit avoir une phase\"\n    assert hasattr(state, 'skills'), \"L'état doit avoir des skills\"\n    \n    return state\n\ndef test_state_loading_basic(initial_state):\n    \"\"\"Test basique du chargement d'état.\"\"\"\n    assert initial_state is not None\n    assert hasattr(initial_state, 'iteration')\n    assert initial_state.iteration >= 0\n\ndef test_state_attributes_exist(initial_state):\n    \"\"\"Test que les attributs critiques existent.\"\"\"\n    required_attrs = ['iteration', 'phase', 'skills', 'learnings']\n    for attr in required_attrs:\n        assert hasattr(initial_state, attr), f\"Attribut manquant: {attr}\"\n\ndef test_state_manager_integration():\n    \"\"\"Test d'intégration du StateManager.\"\"\"\n    manager = StateManager()\n    state = manager.load_state()\n    \n    assert state is not None\n    assert isinstance(state.iteration, int)\n    \n    # Test save/load cycle\n    original_iteration = state.iteration\n    state.iteration += 1\n    manager.save_state(state)\n    \n    reloaded_state = manager.load_state()\n    # Note: avec le stub, on ne peut pas tester la persistance réelle\n    assert reloaded_state is not None\n```\n\n```bash\npytest tests/test_integration.py -v --collect-only\n```",
